                <pb facs="0675" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">781.003/280a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Casablanca</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Goold</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-12T18:00:00-04:00">September 12, 1939—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. For Childs. Despite the uncertainty regarding treaty negotiations in the near
                    future, the Department assumes you are collecting the information required for
                    such negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
